# November 24, 2026: Carnegie libraries of Philadelphia, a batch of the pass the owner asked for to put the buildings
# Andrew Carnegie paid for on the map. Philadelphia got one grant of $1,500,000 in January 1903 and built 25 branch
# libraries from it between 1905 and 1930. This batch: 23 of them, standing, changed or gone; Nicetown and Wissahickon
# are leads in the note. Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia's list as raw text; the Philadelphia Historical
# Commission's 2020 nomination of the Carnegie Libraries Thematic Historic District; Ken Finkel's architectural census
# of the 25 branches (PhillyHistory blog, 2019); the Encyclopedia of Greater Philadelphia; the Free Library's own branch
# pages (hours, histories); city Rebuild pages, local papers and history pages, read through the web fetch tool.
# Pins: ArcGIS geocoder points for the street addresses, or OpenStreetMap points, looked at on the leaf-off aerial.
