  GRANT+' Opened on December 30, 1925, with Carnegie money for the building and $10,000 from the neighbourhood for books. The nomination names Edmund B. Gilchrist as architect; the 2019 census of the branches lists the architect as unknown. Renamed in 1990 for Blanche Nixon, a local activist and library volunteer. An $8.5 million rebuild added a ramp, a lift, an outdoor amphitheatre and a play area, and the branch reopened in spring 2025.',
  'A late one, stripped classical going on Streamline Moderne: stucco over steel and cinder block, with terra cotta, at 59th Street and Baltimore Avenue. Open to anyone in its hours.',
