  GRANT+' Opened on December 3, 1915, the eighteenth of the city\'s Carnegie buildings, on land given by Alex Simpson Jr. The library names Albert Kelsey as architect; the city\'s nomination names Kelsey with Paul Cret. The Old Academy Bell, from a school a block away, is in the reading room. Renovated in 2001; in 2008 it was one of the Carnegie branches the city planned to close. On the Philadelphia Register on its own since 2009.',
  'Colonial Revival in brick on a stone base, with a coloured terra-cotta arch round the door, at 65th Street and Girard Avenue. Open to anyone in its hours.',
