  GRANT+' Opened on November 29, 1919, the twenty-second of the Carnegie branches, on the old playing field of the Belmont Cricket Club. Designed by Philip H. Johnson, who also did the last branch, Wyoming. An $8 million rebuild restored the masonry, kept the old front and added a lift; it reopened in April 2025. On the Philadelphia Register on its own since 2009.',
  'Understated Beaux-Arts in brick on a granite base, with limestone trim, at 51st Street and Kingsessing Avenue. Open to anyone in its hours.',
