  GRANT+' Opened on November 20, 1906, as the Lehigh Avenue branch; the Free Library says it was then the largest library in Pennsylvania. Designed by G. W. and W. D. Hewitt. A plan to move the branch in the mid-1960s was dropped and the building was rehabilitated in 1967; its chandeliers were restored in 1997. Renamed for Lillian Marrero, a librarian here for many years, who died in 2005.',
  'A grand Beaux-Arts front at 6th Street and Lehigh Avenue. The library calls it white limestone; the city\'s nomination describes terra-cotta walls on a limestone base, with marble. Still a branch, open to anyone in its hours.',
