  GRANT+' Opened in February 1909 on land given by John F. S. Morris, to designs by Benjamin Rush Stevens; the city\'s nomination calls it one of the more elaborate of the branches. It closed as a library in the 1960s, when the new Roxborough branch opened, and was sold in 1969. It became a senior centre (the encyclopedia says a nursing home) and in 2012 and 2013 was made into apartments, with dormers added on the roof.',
