  GRANT+' The Passyunk branch opened on April 14, 1914, on land from the Stephen Girard estate, in what is now the Girard Estate neighbourhood. Designed by John T. Windrim. The W.P.A. relandscaped the grounds in 1939. Murals inside by Calvin Jones show Franklin, Girard and Carnegie. Renamed in 2004. On the Philadelphia Register on its own since 1999.',
