  GRANT+' The cornerstone was laid in 1908 and it opened on March 15, 1910, on land given by Anne W. Penfield. Designed by Edward L. Tilton, an architect who specialised in Carnegie libraries. It closed late in 2024 when the heating failed and ceilings came down under a stalled roof job; a $2.5 million rebuild with a new tile roof reopened it in September 2025.',
