  GRANT+' Opened in November 1912 on land given by the Young Men\'s Institute, to designs by David Knickerbacker Boyd. It is the only one of the city\'s Carnegie branches that is nearly square rather than a T. The branch moved in 1963 to a new building at 7th and Carpenter Streets, now the Charles Santore Library. The city\'s nomination lists it as a community centre; the Greater Philadelphia Overseas Chinese Association gives this address. On the Philadelphia Register on its own since 2017.',
