  GRANT+' Opened on June 26, 1907, as the Thomas Holme branch, named for William Penn\'s surveyor-general; designed by Horace W. Castor. The trustees of the Lower Dublin Academy deeded the land in 1905 from a Holme family school fund, on condition that it goes back to them if it ever stops being a library. Often called the smallest of the city\'s branches. On the closing list in 2008 and reprieved.',
